Spec: Caller-bound durable public connections

Purpose:
  Preserve formal connection operations, cumulative snapshots and one-use attachment claims alongside application authority.

Owns:
  ./ConnectionJournal.java

References:
  ./AgentRegistry.sdd
  ./ConnectionMeter.sdd
  /docs/adr/0024-public-connection-lifecycle.md

Must:
  Allow coalesced snapshots to skip forward through pending/attaching/open/draining while rejecting reverse progress; slow half-closed streams must retain observed counters before termination.
  Resolve actual caller ownership, current local device/service grant and requested policy under the same write transaction that records a new open.
  Retain matching operations without dialing again and reject parameter conflicts before changing connection state.
  Bound combined experimental/formal active counts and preserve reserved revocation capacity.
  Persist cumulative snapshots by increasing sequence and original boot; reject stale updates, state regression, path changes or decreasing counters and never revive a terminal record.
  Bind attachment claims and one-use consumption to caller, current boot and current exact authority; a repeated operation returns its original reference without granting another descriptor.
  Recover old active rows in bounded batches, preserving original counters/path and marking unobserved tails incomplete.
